<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Italian War of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1859</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Italian War of Independence was fought in 1859 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a>. Austrian defeats at Magenta and Solferino led to the loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> place it among the defeats that pushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy towards the reforms and compromise that created Austria-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-italian-war-of-independence.jpg" alt="Second Italian War of Independence" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adolphe Yvon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yvon_Bataille_de_Solferino_Compiegne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
